ng  really eager to see the type of feedback  they get most people who are data  scientists within research groups don't  have the opportunity to interact with  this constellation of people  and sir able to not only have a really  great interaction you're able to create  a process where people are Eagle eager  to continue to interact with their  critics so those things of standards  applications and community of practice  within an organization within a team  that one is building basically comes  down to be having training having  quality control and having a team  building process and so we build this in  a large open source community but within  within an analytics team across  especially multiple analytics teams  within an organization incorporating  processes like this can help you drive  all of these things within an  organization so one of the questions is  how do you do this type of review well  both as an organizer or as an individual  reviewer and that's something that we've  been slowly trying to understand an  extract wisdom from our reviewers  because it's often one of these you know  a good one when you see it type things  which is difficult to understand what  the process of a good reviewer is but  it's something we're just beginning to  pull out and understand and so far these  are some of the highlights we think of  the good practices when one is building  a review system or doing a review now  that we've had something like 250  packages in the are open size system go  through this and I think six in the pie  open sigh that just started this year so  the first important thing when one is  doing review is to have a shared common  set of standards and it can be daunting  trying to set standards for one's own  work but the important thing is to start  small on the important things and then  steal most of them because there are a  lot of good standards out there that  different groups have developed often  for similar goal  that you might have so both ar